{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the meaning of \"two years.\"</b> In the portion of Ahijeh the Great [= Genesis 10], and it is possible that Peleg was called by this name on the day he was gathered [= died], for Shem lived 500 years after the Flood, and Arpachshad 338 years, and Shelah his son 303, and Eber his son 464, and so all the days of Peleg were 239 years, and they are half the days of his ancestors; also Reu his son lived after him the same number of years as Peleg, and likewise Serug is close to them. And this is the rule: after Peleg there is none who was 239 years old like Peleg except his son alone. And some say that the seventy were the builders of the Tower, and therefore they were scattered into seventy languages. When you count the sons of Shem, also the sons of Japheth, also the sons of Ham, you will find them seventy. And this is not correct, for the explanation of כפתורים and פתרוסים is not two men, and furthermore he did not include Noah and his sons in the count. And according to the opinion of Seder Olam, the builders of the Tower were thousands and myriads."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The phrase 'בפרשת אחי יפת הגדול' (Genesis 10) refers to the Torah portion's opening words; 'הגדול' likely modifies Japheth as 'the elder,' though the construction is slightly unusual."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:16.944412927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}